        "timestamp": 1773602486
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><img alt=\"Screenshot 2026-03-15 at 3.47.47 PM.png\" class=\"inline-image\" data-original-content-type=\"image/png\" data-original-dimensions=\"1040x1124\" data-original-src=\"/user_uploads/3121/0WSACHjoXftDIBNRmxPSdsVH/Screenshot-2026-03-15-at-3.47.47-PM.png\" src=\"/user_uploads/thumbnail/3121/0WSACHjoXftDIBNRmxPSdsVH/Screenshot-2026-03-15-at-3.47.47-PM.png/840x560.webp\"><br>\n<img alt=\"Screenshot 2026-03-15 at 3.47.58 PM.png\" class=\"inline-image\" data-original-content-type=\"image/png\" data-original-dimensions=\"1030x1160\" data-original-src=\"/user_uploads/3121/OnjhcGRh-BdOkJl1d2vsLjQy/Screenshot-2026-03-15-at-3.47.58-PM.png\" src=\"/user_uploads/thumbnail/3121/OnjhcGRh-BdOkJl1d2vsLjQy/Screenshot-2026-03-15-at-3.47.58-PM.png/840x560.webp\"><br>\nOne is of type <code>UnitAddTorus ι → ↑{x | ∀ (i : ι), x i ∈ Ioc (b i) (b i + 1)}</code> and the other one is of type <code>UnitAddTorus ι → { x // ∀ (i : ι), x i ∈ Ioc (b i) (b i + 1) }</code>.</p>",
        "id": 579571032,
        "sender_full_name": "Yongxi Lin (Aaron)",
        "timestamp": 1773604159
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>And what's the type of <code>↑</code>? I don't know the type of anything here. Oh -- one is a set coerced to a type, the other is a subtype I guess (I had to do the diff manually :-) )</p>",
        "id": 579573461,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1773607060
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Why don't you change the offending definition then?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">measurableEquivPiIoc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">UnitAddTorus</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃ᵐ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ioc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>You are making a set and then immediately coercing it to a subtype -- why not make the RHS simpler by using a subtype directly?</p>",
        "id": 579573534,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1773607183
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"110038\">@Kevin Buzzard</span> Thank you for your suggestions. Using subtypes resolves all the issues.</p>",
